WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.097 --> 00:00:03.667
OF A WASHINGTON STATE FLORIST

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:07.204
WHO DECLINED WHEN A LONG-TIME

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.838
CUSTOMER OF HERS ASKED HER TO DO

00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:08.205
FLOWERS FOR HIS SAME-SEX

00:00:07.971 --> 00:00:10.374
CEREMONY.

00:00:08.338 --> 00:00:12.642
LET'S TALK ABOUT THE LEGAL

00:00:10.507 --> 00:00:13.243
ARGUMENTS.

00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:13.910
SENIOR CLINICAL ANALYST

00:00:13.377 --> 00:00:15.846
BRIT HUME JOINS US TONIGHT.

00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:16.780
GOOD EVENING.

00:00:15.979 --> 00:00:18.448
YOUR REACTION TO THIS RULING.

00:00:16.913 --> 00:00:21.251
&gt;&gt; I THINK YOU ARE CORRECT WHEN

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:23.887
YOU SUGGEST THAT WHILE IT'S NOT

00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:24.921
AN NARROW VOTE, IT'S AN NARROW

00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:27.157
HOLDING IN THE SENSE THAT IT

00:00:25.055 --> 00:00:31.061
APPLIES FOR INSTANCE IN WHICH

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:32.662
THE COURT FOUND THAT THIS BAKER

00:00:31.194 --> 00:00:33.296
DIDN'T GET A FAIR HEARING.

00:00:32.796 --> 00:00:34.898
THE COLORADO CIVIL RIGHTS

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:39.503
COMMISSION WAS SO BIASED AGAINST

00:00:35.032 --> 00:00:43.373
HIM AND BIASED AGAINST THE

00:00:39.636 --> 00:00:44.141
BAKER'S RELIGIOUS CONVICTIONS

00:00:43.507 --> 00:00:47.044
AND BELITTLED THOSE CONVICTIONS,

00:00:44.274 --> 00:00:48.779
DESCRIBING THE ARGUMENT AS

00:00:47.177 --> 00:00:49.946
DESPICABLE, THAT IT WASN'T A

00:00:48.912 --> 00:00:51.281
FAIR HEARING AND COULDN'T STAND

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.882
PRETTY GIVE SOME RECOGNITION TO

00:00:51.415 --> 00:00:54.651
THE IDEA THAT RELIGIOUS

00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:58.155
CONVICTIONS MAY BE A REASON TO

00:00:54.785 --> 00:00:58.855
DENY SERVICES IN CERTAIN

00:00:58.288 --> 00:01:00.023
CIRCUMSTANCES.

00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:02.459
WE DON'T KNOW WHAT THOSE

00:01:00.157 --> 00:01:03.226
CIRCUMSTANCES MIGHT BE.

00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:05.562
A BIT OF FLORIST CASE WILL TELL

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.664
US MORE.

00:01:05.695 --> 00:01:09.266
&gt;&gt; Shannon: TO THE OTHER LEGAL

00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:11.468
ISSUES, THERE PRESIDENT AND

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:11.802
WHETHER OR NOT HE CAN PARDON

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.470
HIMSELF.

00:01:11.935 --> 00:01:14.538
THE CONSTITUTION DOESN'T SAY

00:01:13.603 --> 00:01:17.441
ANYTHING ABOUT THAT BUT HE'S

00:01:14.671 --> 00:01:18.175
GETTING A WARNING FROM HIS OWN

00:01:17.574 --> 00:01:20.777
TOP LAWYER.

00:01:18.308 --> 00:01:21.278
&gt;&gt; RUDY GIULIANI WAS SAYING

00:01:20.911 --> 00:01:26.049
YESTERDAY.

00:01:21.411 --> 00:01:28.185
SAYING IT WOULD BE DISASTROUS.

00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:28.885
HE POINTED OUT THAT IF YOU

00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:32.289
PARDON HIMSELF, PARDONS DON'T

00:01:29.019 --> 00:01:33.924
APPLY TO IMPEACHMENT.

00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:35.158
AND THE QUESTION OF WHETHER HE

00:01:34.057 --> 00:01:38.228
CAN PARDON HIMSELF REMAINS AN

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:39.996
OPEN QUESTION IN THE SENSE THAT

00:01:38.361 --> 00:01:41.064
PARDON POWER IS PRETTY SWEEPING

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:42.999
AND THE PRESIDENT CAN EXERCISE

00:01:41.198 --> 00:01:46.103
IT AS HE SEES FIT.

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:48.839
BUT IT'S NEVER BEEN EXERCISED IN

00:01:46.236 --> 00:01:49.773
A CASE WHERE A PERSON, A

00:01:48.972 --> 00:01:50.907
PRESIDENT IS PARDONING HIMSELF.

00:01:49.906 --> 00:01:52.075
THE CONSTITUTION IS SILENT ON

00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:53.243
IT.

00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:54.044
THERE IS A PRINCIPLE THAT WE

00:01:53.376 --> 00:01:56.546
RECOGNIZE WHICH IS THAT NO

00:01:54.177 --> 00:01:58.515
PERSON SHALL BE THE JUDGE OF HIS

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:59.382
OR HER OWN CASE.

00:01:58.648 --> 00:02:00.717
THIS WOULD SEEM TO FLY IN THE

00:01:59.516 --> 00:02:01.918
FACE OF THAT.

00:02:00.851 --> 00:02:03.086
IT'S A DOUBTFUL PROPOSITION THAT

00:02:02.052 --> 00:02:05.088
HE COULD PARDON HIMSELF.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.123
&gt;&gt; Shannon: IT GOES ALONG WITH

00:02:05.222 --> 00:02:08.692
THE ADVICE THAT YOU SHOULDN'T BE

00:02:06.256 --> 00:02:12.262
YOUR OWN LAWYER.

00:02:08.825 --> 00:02:15.065
YOU CAN'T BE YOUR OWN JUDGE.

00:02:12.395 --> 00:02:18.935
THERE IS THIS ISSUE, 1974

00:02:15.198 --> 00:02:19.503
DECISION CAME FROM WITH IN THE

00:02:19.069 --> 00:02:22.506
DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE.

00:02:19.636 --> 00:02:24.875
&gt;&gt; THIS GOES TO THE QUESTION OF

00:02:22.639 --> 00:02:26.643
WHETHER THE PRESIDENT COULD BE

00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:28.211
INDICTED BY ROBERT MILLER.

00:02:26.776 --> 00:02:31.348
IN THE NIXON ERA, THE JUSTICE

00:02:28.345 --> 00:02:34.651
DEPARTMENT, LEGAL COUNSEL,

00:02:31.481 --> 00:02:36.586
JUSTICE DEPARTMENT IN-HOUSE

00:02:34.784 --> 00:02:37.287
ATTORNEY DETERMINE THAT A

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.688
PRESIDENT, A SITTING PRESIDENT

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.690
COULD NOT BE INDICTED.

00:02:38.822 --> 00:02:42.225
IT WAS LOOKED AT IN 2,000 BY THE

00:02:40.991 --> 00:02:44.394
SAME OFFICE OF LEGAL COUNSEL,

00:02:42.359 --> 00:02:45.695
DIFFERENT PEOPLE CAME TO THE

00:02:44.528 --> 00:02:46.796
SAME CONCLUSION.

00:02:45.829 --> 00:02:47.797
THE JUSTICE DEPARTMENT OFFERED

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.498
LEGAL OPINIONS LIKE THAT ARE NOT

00:02:47.931 --> 00:02:50.667
BINDING LAW.

00:02:48.632 --> 00:02:51.067
THEY ARE BINDING ON THE

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.269
DEPARTMENT.

00:02:51.201 --> 00:02:53.136
SINCE ROBERT MUELLER IS A

00:02:52.402 --> 00:02:55.172
CREATURE OF THAT DEPARTMENT, NOT

00:02:54.104 --> 00:02:56.406
AN INDEPENDENT COUNSEL, SPECIAL

00:02:55.305 --> 00:02:57.908
COUNSEL WORKING FOR THE JUSTICE

00:02:56.606 --> 00:03:00.377
DEPARTMENT, PRESUMABLY THOSE

00:02:58.041 --> 00:03:00.644
OPINIONS WOULD BE BINDING UPON

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:02.946
HIM.

00:03:00.777 --> 00:03:04.247
THAT DOES NOT MEAN THAT IF THE

00:03:03.079 --> 00:03:06.183
PRESIDENT WAS DETERMINED BY THE

00:03:04.381 --> 00:03:10.453
SPECIAL COUNSEL 12 COMMITTED

00:03:06.316 --> 00:03:11.788
SOME CRIME FOR WHICH HE COULD BE

00:03:10.587 --> 00:03:12.255
IMPEACHED, HE COULD THEN BE

00:03:11.922 --> 00:03:14.591
INDICTED.

00:03:12.656 --> 00:03:16.860
IF HE WAS FOUND TO HAVE

00:03:14.724 --> 00:03:18.595
OBSTRUCTED JUSTICE, ONCE HE IS

00:03:16.993 --> 00:03:20.897
IMPEACHED, HE'S NOT IN OFFICE

00:03:18.728 --> 00:03:22.432
AND THE OPINION DOESN'T APPLY.

00:03:21.031 --> 00:03:24.000
HE COULD BE TRIED.

00:03:22.566 --> 00:03:25.669
&gt;&gt; Shannon: THOSE ARE THE LEFT

00:03:24.134 --> 00:03:27.270
RAISING THE CRY SAYING THAT HE'S

00:03:25.802 --> 00:03:28.672
AN IMPERIALIST, HE'S GOING TO DO

00:03:27.404 --> 00:03:30.874
EVERYTHING FOR HIMSELF AND

00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:31.741
PARDON HIMSELF, THE CONSTITUTION

00:03:31.007 --> 00:03:33.543
WIDELY PROVIDES HIM THAT.

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:34.444
&gt;&gt; THE ARGUMENT BEING MADE THAT

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:36.479
THE PRESIDENT IS DECLARING

00:03:34.578 --> 00:03:37.414
HIMSELF ABOVE THE LAW.

00:03:36.613 --> 00:03:38.281
IMPEACHMENT IS A CORE PART OF

00:03:37.547 --> 00:03:41.451
THE LAW.

00:03:38.415 --> 00:03:42.919
SO LONG AS HE IS VULNERABLE,

00:03:41.585 --> 00:03:44.287
SUSCEPTIBLE, SUBJECT TO

00:03:43.053 --> 00:03:44.554
IMPEACHMENT, HE'S NOT ABOVE THE

00:03:44.421 --> 00:03:46.923
LAW.

00:03:44.688 --> 00:03:48.992
&gt;&gt; Shannon: HE AND HIS

00:03:47.057 --> 00:03:49.359
ATTORNEYS MAINTAIN IT'S A MOOT

00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:50.060
QUESTION.

00:03:49.492 --> 00:03:52.896
HE HAS DONE NOTHING WRONG AND

00:03:50.193 --> 00:03:53.663
THEY ARE CONFIDENT THAT'S WHAT

00:03:53.029 --> 00:03:55.031
THE SPECIAL COUNSEL WILL FIND

00:03:53.797 --> 00:03:55.332
GREAT &gt;&gt; I THINK IT'S THE SILLY

00:03:55.165 --> 00:04:01.371
ISSUE.

00:03:55.465 --> 00:04:02.105
THE BIG IT'S GOING TO HAPPEN.

00:04:01.504 --> 00:04:03.506
COULD BE CALAMITOUS POLITICALLY.

00:04:02.239 --> 00:04:05.508
&gt;&gt; Shannon: I THINK IT WAS

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:08.078
THAT CHAIR OF THE SENATE

